{"qid":"Q55","names":["Netherlands"],"title":"Netherlands","endonym":{"native":"Nederland","lang":"nl"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of the Netherlands in its modern form dates to 1815, following the Napoleonic period during which the country was annexed directly into France (1810–1813); the dataset's from-date of 1811 reflects peak French administrative incorporation. After the Belgian secession (1830–1839), the Netherlands settled into its current northern borders and developed a major colonial empire centered on the Dutch East Indies (modern Indonesia), which declared independence in 1945 (recognized 1949). A founding member of NATO (1949) and the European Community (1957), the Netherlands is a constitutional monarchy under the House of Orange-Nassau.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Metropolitan borders are precisely known throughout the modern period; colonial possessions had well-documented boundaries established by treaties, though administrative control varied.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Netherlands","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands"},{"label":"Britannica: Netherlands","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Netherlands"},{"label":"Britannica: History of the Netherlands","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Netherlands/History"}],"britannica":"place/Netherlands","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Netherlands","rulers":[{"qid":"Q107861327","name":"Jacob Pruijs","start":1811,"end":1830,"image":null},{"qid":"Q3500301","name":"Arend François van den Steen","start":1816,"end":1830,"image":"Arend Francois van den Steen (1766-1842).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.or